Subject: Cantor Self Work Update Broker B0 Protocol Data And Dual Review

@ [review_uuid] cad08d1c-f705-47ca-899e-66cc4957ed9f
@ [canonical_uuid] 6745420e-60dc-4ed6-8c1f-3b143971a814

& [DataDesign]
  + strict public metadata types make all lineage stage capability evidence unresolved output and fault facts inspectable
  + exact enums eliminate generic stage capability disposition and authority escapes
  + six-stage and twenty-three-capability cardinalities are validated structurally
  + all hashes are domain-separated complete canonical self-excluding JSON
  + no runtime handle or carrier type exists in the module

& [ConstructiveHemisphere]
  + B0 can make the future physical broker plan machine-checkable before any process or filesystem contact
  + exhaustive explicit denial proves the protocol validator itself grants nothing
  + deterministic replay provides a stable substrate for later separately signed stages

& [CriticalHemisphere]
  + a generic receipt could smuggle a later physical result
  + a generic capability string could hide an unreviewed effect
  + synthetic evidence could be mislabeled live
  + a valid result could be misread as activation authority
  + deserialization could be abused to construct a runtime carrier if one existed

& [Resolution]
  + no generic receipt or later-stage result type exists
  + closed enum plus exact exhaustive denied list replaces strings
  + evidence requires physical_contact false and output repeats false
  + exact nonauthority and FormationOnly are validated on replay
  + runtime carrier callback constructor global lookup and effect import are statically absent

& [APIReview]
  + one compile function request and result validators digest helpers and strict machine-form helpers are sufficient
  + all functions accept owned metadata references or bytes and return metadata or typed fault
  + no trait object closure callback path executable or host parameter exists

& [Decision]
  + twenty constraints fourteen threats and seven folds close with zero gap
  + exact one-module implementation is feasible with current dependencies
  + physical and downstream authority remain absent
